# Telco Customer Churn Analysis

## Overview

A data analysis project investigating customer churn patterns for a telecommunications company. The project uses SQL to explore customer behavior, identify key churn drivers, and develop business insights for customer retention.

## Business Objective

Identify customer segments and factors associated with higher churn and translate the findings into actionable retention opportunities.

## Tools

* **MySQL** — Data preparation, validation, exploratory analysis, cross-analysis, and SQL JOIN analysis
* **GitHub** — Version control and project documentation
* **Power BI** — Interactive dashboard and business visualization *(upcoming)*

## Analysis

The SQL analysis covers:

* Data validation and quality checks
* Customer and financial profiling
* Churn analysis by contract, payment method, tenure, and services
* Cross-analysis of key churn factors
* JOIN-based analysis comparing customer segments
* Business insights and retention recommendations

## Key Findings

* Month-to-month customers have substantially higher churn than customers on longer-term contracts.
* Electronic-check customers show higher churn across all contract types.
* Churned customers have higher average monthly charges than retained customers across all contract types.
* Several customer and service characteristics are associated with elevated churn and may warrant targeted retention strategies.

## Next Phase

The SQL analysis will be used as the foundation for a Power BI dashboard focused on interactive churn analysis and business storytelling.